  <p>This loop is simple enough to fit in a diagram, but most of the engineering is hidden inside the boxes. What counts as an observation? Which files are included? How are tool schemas described? How are screenshots translated into model-readable state? What happens when the model calls the wrong tool? Who approves dangerous commands? How is the conversation compacted when the context window fills up? How does the system recover after a failed edit?</p>

  <p>Those questions are the harness. The LLM is important, but the harness defines the world the LLM inhabits.</p>

  <h2>The Five Layers</h2>

  <p>A useful way to understand modern harnesses is to split them into five layers:</p>

